---
import CorrectionDraft from '../components/CorrectionDraft.astro';
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
const issueURL=(title:string,body:string)=>'https://github.com/ahimanikya/utkal-project/issues/new?'+new URLSearchParams({title,body});
const knowledgeURL=issueURL('[Knowledge] Suggest a new subject', 'Subject and place:\n\nWhat could this entry help readers understand?\n\nSources or firsthand context (label uncertainty and recollections):\n\nRequested public credit (optional):\n\nThis proposal is public on GitHub. Do not include private information. Posting does not imply editorial acceptance or publication.');
const photoURL=issueURL('[Photo] Photograph proposal', 'Subject and place:\n\nCaption and approximate date:\n\nCreator and public source:\n\nLicence or proposed reuse permission:\n\nEditing, including any AI generation:\n\nRequested public credit (optional):\n\nOnly attach material you have permission to share publicly. Do not attach private permission letters. Editors must verify rights before reuse; posting is not encyclopedia publication.');
---
<Shell title="Be part of the story" active="contribute"><div class="wrap"><div class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">An invitation to contribute</p><h1>What do you know<br/>that we should know?</h1><p class="lead">A place remembered. A photograph with a story. A better source. Every thoughtful contribution can deepen the record.</p></div><div class="prose section" style="padding-top:0"><p class="notice">Our first contribution channel is public GitHub Issues. Prepare a draft below, then review and submit it on GitHub. This website does not upload or store your draft. A GitHub account is needed; your username, text and attachments are public when posted.</p><h2>Share knowledge</h2><p>Help document a place, a person, a craft or a local word. Tell us how you know it and include sources where available. Personal recollections are welcome as recollections, rather than presented as established historical fact.</p><p><a class="text-link" href={knowledgeURL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Propose a new subject on GitHub ↗</a></p><h2>Share photographs</h2><p>Prepare a caption, location, approximate date and the credit you would like used. Share only images you have permission to offer. You may propose a publicly shareable photograph through a GitHub issue. Identify the creator and licence or permission; do not post private images, personal documents or restricted community material.</p><p><a class="text-link" href={photoURL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Propose a photograph on GitHub ↗</a></p><h2>Improve an entry</h2><p>Keep the entry’s title, the suggested correction and a supporting source together. Approved Git contributors will also be able to propose changes through the repository.</p><h2>What happens next?</h2><ol class="contribution-steps"><li><strong>Prepare:</strong> name the entry, proposed change, evidence and requested credit.</li><li><strong>Submit on GitHub:</strong> check the public preview and choose “Submit new issue”.</li><li><strong>Review:</strong> the editor checks sources, rights and context, and may ask follow-up questions.</li><li><strong>Decide:</strong> the Founder & Editor-in-Chief approves, requests changes or declines with a reason.</li><li><strong>Publish:</strong> accepted work links back to its issue and preserves agreed credit. Closing an issue alone does not mean publication.</li></ol><p>Editors will review submissions, clarify attribution and permissions, and decide what is ready to publish. A submitted issue is public immediately on GitHub. Its contents appear in the encyclopedia only after editorial review and approval.</p><a class="text-link" href="/explore/">Explore what we’re building ↗</a></div><CorrectionDraft/></div></Shell>
